# "Can't be blocked by more than one creature" (CR 509.1b): Bot1 attacks with Edge Rover, enchanted by Meltstrider's Resolve,
# and an unenchanted Elvish Mystic. Bot2 may not put two of its creatures in front of the Rover, while two may block the Mystic
# together (the positive control) and one alone may block the Rover. The Rover (2/4) kills the Curious Farm Animals and keeps 1
# damage; the Mystic, double-blocked, deals its 1 to the Haywire Mite and dies.

[Bot1 Deck]
Forest
Edge Rover
Forest
Elvish Mystic
Meltstrider's Resolve
Forest x15

[Bot2 Deck]
Plains
Mox Pearl
Curious Farm Animals
Haywire Mite
Ornithopter
Plains x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Edge Rover.Cast
[T2 Bot2.Main1]
Bot2.Hand.Plains.Play
Bot2.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Plains.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Curious Farm Animals.Cast
Bot2.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot2.Hand.Haywire Mite.Cast
Bot2.Hand.Ornithopter.Cast
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Hand.Forest.Play
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#1.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Elvish Mystic.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Forest#2.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Meltstrider's Resolve.Cast(Edge Rover)
Bot1.Pass
Bot2.Pass
Bot1.Target()
[T5 Bot1.DeclareAttackers]
Bot1.Attack(Edge Rover; Elvish Mystic > Bot2)
! Bot2.Block(Curious Farm Animals > Edge Rover; Haywire Mite > Edge Rover)
! Bot2.Block(Curious Farm Animals > Edge Rover; Ornithopter > Edge Rover)
Bot2.Block(Curious Farm Animals > Edge Rover; Haywire Mite > Elvish Mystic; Ornithopter > Elvish Mystic)
? Combat.Blocks = Curious Farm Animals > Edge Rover; Haywire Mite > Elvish Mystic; Ornithopter > Elvish Mystic
Bot1.AssignDamage(Elvish Mystic > Haywire Mite: 1)
[T5 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Bot2.Graveyard = Haywire Mite; Curious Farm Animals
Bot1.Graveyard = Elvish Mystic
Bot1.Battlefield.Edge Rover.Damage = 1
Bot2.Life = 25
